With SELinux built in (vendor/oneplus 0004), init could not start five sdm845 services: their configs name SELinux
domains that OH's policy does not define (u:r:pd-mapper:s0, rmtfs, tqftpserv, qpower_sa, timekeep_sa), so setting
the domain failed ("failed to set secon", exit 21) and init gave up after its retries. Without pd-mapper and rmtfs
the modem and the audio DSP's services never come up: no Wi-Fi, no sound card, no GNSS.

The configs drop "secon"; init runs the services in OH's default domain for services without one (limit_domain).
Their own domains would be needed for enforcing mode.

diff --git a/sdm845/systemability/pd-mapper/pd-mapper.cfg b/sdm845/systemability/pd-mapper/pd-mapper.cfg
index 6895f8b..da6b97a 100644
--- a/sdm845/systemability/pd-mapper/pd-mapper.cfg
+++ b/sdm845/systemability/pd-mapper/pd-mapper.cfg
@@ -3,8 +3,7 @@
             "name" : "pd-mapper",
             "path" : ["/system/bin/pd-mapper"],
             "uid" : "root",
-            "gid" : ["root", "shell"],
-            "secon" : "u:r:pd-mapper:s0"
+            "gid" : ["root", "shell"]
         }
     ]
 }
\ No newline at end of file
